{"id":16,"slug":"16-semantic-html-la-gi-tai-sao-quan-trong","category":"HTML","subcategory":"Semantic","level":"beginner","question_vi":"Semantic HTML là gì? Tại sao quan trọng?","question_en":"What is semantic HTML? Why does it matter?","answer_vi":"Semantic HTML là dùng thẻ **mô tả đúng vai trò nội dung** thay vì `<div>`/`<span>` trung tính.\n\n```html\n<!-- không semantic -->\n<div class=\"header\">\n  <div class=\"nav\">...</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"content\">\n  <div class=\"post\">...</div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- semantic -->\n<header>\n  <nav>...</nav>\n</header>\n<main>\n  <article>...</article>\n</main>\n```\n\nBốn lý do nó đáng giá:\n1. **Accessibility** — screen reader nhảy thẳng tới landmark (`main`, `nav`, `header`); với `<div>` thì không có gì để nhảy tới.\n2. **SEO** — search engine hiểu đâu là nội dung chính, đâu là điều hướng.\n3. **Bảo trì** — đọc cấu trúc là hiểu, không phải dò tên class.\n4. **Hành vi mặc định** — `<button>` có sẵn focus, Enter/Space, trạng thái disabled; `<div onclick>` phải tự làm lại tất cả.\n\n**Chốt:** thẻ semantic bị hỏi nhiều nhất trong phỏng vấn không phải `<article>` mà là `<button>` vs `<div onclick>` — trả lời được ý số 4 là ăn điểm.","answer_en":"Semantic HTML means using tags that **describe the role of the content** instead of neutral `<div>`/`<span>`.\n\n```html\n<!-- not semantic -->\n<div class=\"header\">\n  <div class=\"nav\">...</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"content\">\n  <div class=\"post\">...</div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- semantic -->\n<header>\n  <nav>...</nav>\n</header>\n<main>\n  <article>...</article>\n</main>\n```\n\nFour reasons it pays off:\n1. **Accessibility** — a screen reader can jump straight to a landmark (`main`, `nav`, `header`); with `<div>` there is nothing to jump to.\n2. **SEO** — search engines can tell the main content from the navigation.\n3. **Maintainability** — the structure reads as documentation; no need to decode class names.\n4. **Built-in behavior** — `<button>` already has focus, Enter/Space handling and a disabled state; `<div onclick>` has to reimplement all of it.\n\n**Takeaway:** the semantic element interviewers ask about most is not `<article>` but `<button>` vs `<div onclick>` — point 4 is what earns the mark.","answer_html_vi":"<p>Semantic HTML là dùng thẻ <strong>mô tả đúng vai trò nội dung</strong> thay vì <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;span&gt;</code> trung tính.</p><div class=\"qa-code-wrap\"><span class=\"qa-code-lang\">html</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"qa-code-copy\" data-code=\"&lt;!-- không semantic --&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;header&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;nav&quot;&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;post&quot;&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;!-- semantic --&gt;\n&lt;header&gt;\n  &lt;nav&gt;...&lt;/nav&gt;\n&lt;/header&gt;\n&lt;main&gt;\n  &lt;article&gt;...&lt;/article&gt;\n&lt;/main&gt;\" aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg class=\"qa-code-copy-icon-default\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"/><path d=\"M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1\"/></svg><svg class=\"qa-code-copy-icon-done\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"/></svg><span class=\"qa-code-copy-label-default\">Copy</span><span class=\"qa-code-copy-label-done\">Copied</span></button><pre class=\"qa-code-pre\"><code class=\"qa-code-block hljs\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\">&lt;!-- không semantic --&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span> <span class=\"hljs-attr\">class</span>=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;header&quot;</span>&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span> <span class=\"hljs-attr\">class</span>=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;nav&quot;</span>&gt;</span>...<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span>&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span>&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span> <span class=\"hljs-attr\">class</span>=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;content&quot;</span>&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span> <span class=\"hljs-attr\">class</span>=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;post&quot;</span>&gt;</span>...<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span>&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span>&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">&lt;!-- semantic --&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">header</span>&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">nav</span>&gt;</span>...<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">nav</span>&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">header</span>&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">main</span>&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">article</span>&gt;</span>...<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">article</span>&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">main</span>&gt;</span></code></pre></div><p class=\"qa-summary\">Bốn lý do nó đáng giá:<br/>1. <strong>Accessibility</strong> — screen reader nhảy thẳng tới landmark (<code>main</code>, <code>nav</code>, <code>header</code>); với <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> thì không có gì để nhảy tới.<br/>2. <strong>SEO</strong> — search engine hiểu đâu là nội dung chính, đâu là điều hướng.<br/>3. <strong>Bảo trì</strong> — đọc cấu trúc là hiểu, không phải dò tên class.<br/>4. <strong>Hành vi mặc định</strong> — <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> có sẵn focus, Enter/Space, trạng thái disabled; <code>&lt;div onclick&gt;</code> phải tự làm lại tất cả.</p><p class=\"qa-detail\"><strong>Chốt:</strong> thẻ semantic bị hỏi nhiều nhất trong phỏng vấn không phải <code>&lt;article&gt;</code> mà là <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> vs <code>&lt;div onclick&gt;</code> — trả lời được ý số 4 là ăn điểm.</p>","answer_html_en":"<p>Semantic HTML means using tags that <strong>describe the role of the content</strong> instead of neutral <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;span&gt;</code>.</p><div class=\"qa-code-wrap\"><span class=\"qa-code-lang\">html</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"qa-code-copy\" data-code=\"&lt;!-- not semantic --&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;header&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;nav&quot;&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;post&quot;&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;!-- semantic --&gt;\n&lt;header&gt;\n  &lt;nav&gt;...&lt;/nav&gt;\n&lt;/header&gt;\n&lt;main&gt;\n  &lt;article&gt;...&lt;/article&gt;\n&lt;/main&gt;\" aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg class=\"qa-code-copy-icon-default\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"/><path d=\"M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1\"/></svg><svg class=\"qa-code-copy-icon-done\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"/></svg><span class=\"qa-code-copy-label-default\">Copy</span><span class=\"qa-code-copy-label-done\">Copied</span></button><pre class=\"qa-code-pre\"><code class=\"qa-code-block hljs\"><span class=\"hljs-comment\">&lt;!-- not semantic --&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span> <span class=\"hljs-attr\">class</span>=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;header&quot;</span>&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span> <span class=\"hljs-attr\">class</span>=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;nav&quot;</span>&gt;</span>...<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span>&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span>&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span> <span class=\"hljs-attr\">class</span>=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;content&quot;</span>&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span> <span class=\"hljs-attr\">class</span>=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;post&quot;</span>&gt;</span>...<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span>&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">div</span>&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\">&lt;!-- semantic --&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">header</span>&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">nav</span>&gt;</span>...<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">nav</span>&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">header</span>&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">main</span>&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;<span class=\"hljs-name\">article</span>&gt;</span>...<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">article</span>&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-tag\">&lt;/<span class=\"hljs-name\">main</span>&gt;</span></code></pre></div><p class=\"qa-summary\">Four reasons it pays off:<br/>1. <strong>Accessibility</strong> — a screen reader can jump straight to a landmark (<code>main</code>, <code>nav</code>, <code>header</code>); with <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> there is nothing to jump to.<br/>2. <strong>SEO</strong> — search engines can tell the main content from the navigation.<br/>3. <strong>Maintainability</strong> — the structure reads as documentation; no need to decode class names.<br/>4. <strong>Built-in behavior</strong> — <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> already has focus, Enter/Space handling and a disabled state; <code>&lt;div onclick&gt;</code> has to reimplement all of it.</p><p class=\"qa-detail\"><strong>Takeaway:</strong> the semantic element interviewers ask about most is not <code>&lt;article&gt;</code> but <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> vs <code>&lt;div onclick&gt;</code> — point 4 is what earns the mark.</p>","references":[{"label":"ITviec — Top 50+ câu hỏi phỏng vấn HTML CSS","url":"https://itviec.com/blog/cau-hoi-phong-van-html-css/"},{"label":"Viblo — Bộ câu hỏi phỏng vấn Intern/Fresher Front-end","url":"https://viblo.asia/p/bo-cau-hoi-phong-van-intern-fresher-cho-front-end-tu-a-z-Do754rgVZM6"},{"label":"MDN — Semantics (glossary)","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Semantics"}],"related":[{"url":"/q/17-su-khac-biet-giua-div-va-section-la-gi","title":"Sự khác biệt giữa `<div>` và `<section>` là gì?"},{"url":"/q/18-article-va-section-khac-nhau-the-nao","title":"`<article>` và `<section>` khác nhau thế nào?"},{"url":"/q/19-header-footer-nav-main-aside-dung-khi-nao","title":"`<header>`, `<footer>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<aside>` dùng khi nào?"},{"url":"/q/20-figure-va-figcaption-dung-de-lam-gi","title":"`<figure>` và `<figcaption>` dùng để làm gì?"},{"url":"/q/21-mark-strong-em-khac-nhau-the-nao","title":"`<mark>`, `<strong>`, `<em>` khác nhau thế nào?"},{"url":"/q/22-the-time-duoc-su-dung-de-lam-gi","title":"Thẻ `<time>` được sử dụng để làm gì?"},{"url":"/q/23-semantic-html-anh-huong-seo-nhu-the-nao","title":"Semantic HTML ảnh hưởng SEO như thế nào?"},{"url":"/q/24-khi-nao-dung-dl-dt-dd","title":"Khi nào dùng `<dl>`, `<dt>`, `<dd>`?"}]}